# Widget conventions

There are **two patterns** for widgets, depending on what they extend.

## Pattern 1: extend `BaseWidget` directly

Use when the widget needs blessed.Box behavior plus our additions
(focusable, ready promise, bindings, logger):

```js
var BaseWidget = require('./BaseWidget');

class Foo extends BaseWidget {
  constructor(opts) {
    super(_.merge({/* defaults */}, Slap.global.options.foo, opts));
    var self = this;
    // children, fields, etc.
  }

  _initHandlers() {
    var self = this;
    // event wiring
    return super._initHandlers.apply(self, arguments);  // chain to parent
  }
}
```

`Slap`, `Pane`, `EditorPane`, `Header`, `BaseForm`, `BaseFindForm`,
`FindForm`, `GoLineForm`, `SaveAsForm`, `SaveAsCloseForm`, `PaneList` follow
this pattern.

## Pattern 2: extend a built-in blessed widget + mixin

Use when you need a specific blessed widget (Button, List, FileManager,
Text) AND BaseWidget's behavior. ES6 classes can't be called as functions,
so we use a static mixin:

```js
var BaseWidget = require('./BaseWidget');

class Bar extends BaseWidget.blessed.Button {
  constructor(opts) {
    opts = _.merge({/* defaults */}, Slap.global.options.bar, opts);
    super(opts);                              // calls blessed.Button
    BaseWidget._initBaseWidget(this, opts);   // mixes in BaseWidget behavior
  }

  _initHandlers() {
    var self = this;
    // ...
    return BaseWidget.prototype._initHandlers.apply(self, arguments);
  }
}
```

`Button`, `Label`, `FileBrowser`, `PaneList` (its inner `list`) follow this
pattern.

## Logger lookup is defensive

`BaseWidget._initBaseWidget` reads `self.parent`/`self.screen` (set by
blessed in `super(opts)`), NOT `opts.parent`/`opts.screen`. The mixin path
doesn't normalize opts the way the constructor path does. If you ever
duplicate or refactor that lookup, **guard each `.options` deref**:

```js
// ❌ WRONG (blew up at runtime as `b663016`)
var loggerOpts = opts.logger
  || (opts.parent || {}).options.logger     // .options on {} → undefined
  || (opts.screen || {}).options.logger;    // .logger on undefined → throws

// ✅ RIGHT
var parent = self.parent || opts.parent;
var screen = self.screen || opts.screen;
var loggerOpts = opts.logger
  || (parent && parent.options && parent.options.logger)
  || (screen && screen.options && screen.options.logger);
```
